## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical understanding of retrieval pipelines using chunking, embeddings, and vector stores, along with knowledge of real-world metrics for evaluating RAG systems.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)
- Document chunking strategies (size, overlap, and trade-offs)
- Embedding models and vector stores
- Two-stage retrieval (dense retrieval + reranking)
- Evaluation metrics: recall@K and latency benchmarks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal chunking sketch (size=512, overlap=128)
function chunkText(text, size = 512, overlap = 128) {
  const chunks = [];
  let start = 0;
  while (start < text.length) {
    const end = start + size;
    chunks.push(text.slice(start, end));
    start += size - overlap;
  }
  return chunks;
}

// Two-step retrieval call
async function retrieve(query, topK = 10) {
  const queryEmbedding = await embedModel.embed(query);
  const initialResults = await vectorStore.search(queryEmbedding, topK * 3);
  const reranked = await reranker.rerank(query, initialResults, topK);
  return reranked;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Enterprise chat assistants must process multilingual, long-context inputs containing specialized domain terminology while maintaining performance. This question evaluates understanding of tokenizer design, attention mechanisms, and practical engineering trade-offs in production systems.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual subword tokenization with domain-specific vocabulary enhancement
- Sparse attention patterns using local windows and global anchors
- Cross-language semantic alignment and retrieval augmentation
- Latency-accuracy trade-offs in large-scale deployment

## Code Example
```javascript
function buildSparseMask(n, localWin, globalAnchors) {
  const mask = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(false));

  // Local attention windows
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    const start = Math.max(0, i - localWin);
    const end = Math.min(n, i + localWin + 1);
    for (let j = start; j < end; j++) {
      mask[i][j] = true;
    }
  }

  // Global anchor attention
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (const anchor of globalAnchors) {
      mask[i][anchor] = true;
      mask[anchor][i] = true;
    }
  }

  return mask;
}
```

